{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwLbbioAZChMGNNmA9Jg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to see how the panels render, and I haven't checked that the rule runs cleanly or what it matches.\n\n**Data:** the logs index has `timestamp`, `response` (a string, so I used `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `request`, `url` and `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-59285691 Web logs overview\" has four panels, at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-59285691-web-logs-overview-8b9a321178a8\n- Total requests (single number)\n- Requests over time (area chart)\n- Requests by response code (pie chart)\n- Average bytes by extension (bar chart)\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-59285691 5xx spike\" (id `cc6541f6-91df-4f85-a426-7d1917cd0b02`) is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]` over the last 5 minutes. It fires when that count is above 10. It has no action attached, so it only records alerts in Kibana and doesn't notify anyone.\n\nThe rule was created disabled, so I enabled it as a second step."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":20282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161},"output_tokens":471,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"e2a964a3-9b9b-413e-b9cb-8e04b88de7a6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T23:44:32.464Z","request_id":"req_011CfwLbbWPTbbNAxCPaX5gC"}
